SUMMARY:Unkink Your Obstacle: A Workshop
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nHey Nomads!\nLet's face it\, we’ve all g
 ot something. A recurring frustration\, an exhausting pattern\, an issue w
 e’ve tried to resolve a dozen different ways that somehow keeps showing 
 up.\n\nThis is a fresh approach to them—a way to quit working on the sam
 e old problems and start outgrowing them.\n\n**If you could wave a magic w
 and\, what pattern or obstacle in your life would you make disappear? Brin
 g it here.**\n\n*“The greatest and most important problems of life are a
 ll in a certain sense insoluble. … They can never be solved\, but only o
 utgrown.”*\n*— Carl Jung*\n\nJoin fellow ADN member Rachel Bulkley\, f
 ounder of The WellBeing Project\, for an interactive workshop on a differe
 nt approach to the problems that keep us stuck.\n\nTogether\, we’ll look
  under the hood of what makes life suck right now. Or\, if you prefer\, th
 e specific sources of annoying friction in your otherwise perfectly deligh
 tful existence.\n\nWe’ll look at the difference between repeatedly tryin
 g to solve our problems and tending the conditions underneath them.\n\n**W
 ho it's for**\n\n* You’ve tried all the stuff: books\, practices\, thera
 py\, new routines—and still feel like something isn’t clicking.\n* You
 ’re turned off by elite coaching claims and trendy self-help programs\, 
 but you’re interested in understanding yourself and growing healthier.\n
 * You’re curious about human behavior\, the conditions that help us thri
 ve\, and why knowing what to do doesn’t always translate into doing it.\
 n* You enjoy thoughtful conversations with interesting people. Especially 
 when you leave seeing something differently.\n\n**What we'll do**\nWe’ll
  kick off with 15 minutes to mingle\, then get to work. This is an active 
 workshop\, so come with one persistent problem\, pattern\, or source of fr
 ustration in mind.\n\nWe’ll start with a brief grounding exercise\, then
  take an honest look at how you’ve approached your obstacle so far.\n\nF
 rom there\, we’ll step back and look at:\n\n* Some common beliefs about 
 success\, effort\, and care that may be making life unnecessarily difficul
 t.\n* The fundamental needs all humans share\, and what happens when those
  needs go unmet.\n* How The Ten Areas of Human Needs can help us understan
 d what’s underneath our recurring struggles.\n* What becomes possible wh
 en we start tending the conditions that support our growth.\n\nThen we’l
 l return to the obstacle you brought with you and see what looks different
 . We’ll leave time at the end for questions\, and you’re welcome to st
 ick around and socialize after.\n\n**What you'll leave with**\n\n* A fresh
  perspective on a familiar challenge.\n* A clearer understanding of what m
 ight be underneath it.\n* A practical approach to creating healthier condi
 tions in your life.\n* A way of thinking you can apply to other recurring 
 struggles.\n\n**A few things...**\nYour privacy is yours. Most of the refl
 ection happens in your own notebook. You’re welcome to contribute to the
  discussion\, but nobody will be asked to disclose personal details.\n\n**
 Bring:** A notebook\, a pen\, an open mind\, and one frustrating thing you
 ’d happily wave goodbye to.\n\n**Getting there:** We’ll meet in Room 5
  at Hatch Coworking\, 45 South French Broad Ave\, Asheville. Free parking 
 is available behind the building. Before the event\, you’ll get a note w
 ith parking and entry details.\n\n**Come as you are. Bring your obstacle. 
 Let’s see what we can unkink.**
